From afab0aa190b5c900724e57dfa9539c2421baa07a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:01:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.02a: UpdateCheckScheduler + pref names

Pure-policy scheduling primitive for the update-check cadence. No
timer, no I/O, no prefs read inline -- the caller injects a
"is auto-check enabled?" callback and feeds wall-clock time. This
isolates the cadence math (5 min initial; 24h +/- 6h jittered base)
from the keyed-service / pref-store / timer plumbing that plan
10-02b will own.

  * pref_names.h -- prefs::kAutoCheckEnabled (bool, default true),
    kLastCheckTime, kNextCheckTime (int64 microseconds since the
    Windows epoch).
  * update_check_scheduler.{h,cc} -- UpdateCheckScheduler with
    kInitialDelay/kBaseInterval/kJitter constants and
    ComputeNextDelay(is_first_check). Uniform jitter via
    base::RandGenerator (uint64 -> recentered int64 to avoid the
    base::RandInt int-only signature).
  * update_check_scheduler_unittest.cc -- 3 tests:
    ReturnsNulloptWhenAutoCheckDisabled, FirstCheckUsesInitialDelay,
    SubsequentChecksAreJitteredWithinEnvelope (200 draws within
    [base-jitter, base+jitter] with >100 distinct values to catch
    a fully-deterministic regression).
  * BUILD.gn -- new source_set(scheduler), wired into unit_tests.

Build: phlink_updater_unittests OK (7/7 pass; 4 metadata + 3
scheduler), chrome OK (codesigned).

Refs phase 10 plan 10-02a.
